<title>USA: GPU Inc Q1 shr $1.28 vs $0.90.</title>
<headline>GPU Inc Q1 shr $1.28 vs $0.90.</headline>
<dateline>PARSIPPANY, N.J. 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>					  Three Months Ended March 31</p>
<p>							 1997	 1996</p>
<p> Sales to customers (gigawatt-hours)(a)     11,178     11,384</p>
<p> Operating revenues			   $1,042,064 $1,022,934</p>
<p> Net income					  155,038    108,253</p>
<p> Earnings per average share			 1.28	 0.90</p>
<p> Average common shares outstanding	   120,889    120,640</p>
<p>					  Twelve Months Ended March 31</p>
<p>							 1997	 1996</p>
<p> Sales to customers (gigawatt-hours)(a)     42,307     42,171</p>
<p> Operating revenues (000)		    3,937,219  3,913,618</p>
<p> Net income (000) (b) (c)			345,137    472,891</p>
<p> Earnings per average share (b) (c)	     2.85	4.04</p>
<p> Average common shares outstanding	   120,805    117,526</p>
<p>(a)Gigawatt-hour sales exclude interchange sales.</p>
<p>(b)Earnings for the twelve months ended March 31, 1997 include an after-tax charge to income of $74.5 million, or $0.62 per share, for costs related to voluntary enhanced retirement programs.</p>
<p>(c)Earnings for the twelve months ended March 31, 1996 include an after-tax credit to income of $104.9 million, or $0.91 per share, resulting from the reversal of certain future TMI-2 retirement costs previously written off.  Partially offsetting the effect of this increase was an after-tax write- off of $8.4 million, or $0.07 per share, for TMI-2 monitored storage costs.</p>
<p>--((New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
